{
  "about": "Each taboo is an act that the people who care will react to, not one that cannot happen: a taboo is a price, not a wall (Part III 9; Part V 10.4). The reactions are ranges for judging plausibility, not a menu to choose from, and each reaction is individual (Tendency): a boss, a capo and a man who learns of the act each decide for himself. The one exception is in fixed_rules: women are never made, and that carries no price.",
  "source": "Part III 9 (15 rows, Fixed) and Part V 10.4 (8 rows, Fixed); the reaction ranges are Tendency. Wording of the cells follows the bible; a row's cell that was a range 'from X to Y' is split into its ends and steps.",
